[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Today, I\'m excited to introduce another powerful&nbsp; All-in-One workflow for video enhancement. &nbsp; First, it can easily remove unwanted objects&nbsp; like icons, watermarks, and subtitles. &nbsp; Next, it can upscale and restore video&nbsp; quality with impressive results. &nbsp; And finally, it can expand your footage from&nbsp; horizontal to vertical—or the other way around. &nbsp;'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'First, install ComfyUI by following&nbsp; the tutorial on my channel.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then, download all the required models and place&nbsp; them in the appropriate folders. Finally, load the&nbsp;&nbsp; workflow linked in the description below. This is an LTX 2.3 video-to-video workflow&nbsp;&nbsp; featuring six different options. This&nbsp; workflow uses just a single sampler.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Switching between options is handled by dedicated&nbsp; pre-processing modules, which you can explore by&nbsp;&nbsp; opening the subgraphs. This design keeps the&nbsp; workflow lightweight despite its wide range of&nbsp;&nbsp; features, while also significantly reducing&nbsp; the risk of running into memory issues. &nbsp;'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'First, I\'ll load a video. Since this video&nbsp; contains both a watermark and subtitles,&nbsp;&nbsp; I\'ll choose Option 1. Checking the video\'s properties, we can&nbsp;&nbsp; see it runs at 30 FPS, has 621 frames, a duration&nbsp; of 20.7 seconds, and a resolution of 720 × 1280.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For this test, I\'ll process only the first&nbsp; 5 seconds, which is about 125 frames.&nbsp;&nbsp; I\'ll keep the resolution at 1280, but&nbsp; reduce the frame rate to 25 FPS to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'speed up the generation. Then, I\'ll click Run. The Sampler subgraph automatically enables the&nbsp;&nbsp; LoRA modules designed to remove both the watermark&nbsp; and subtitles before reconstructing the video. &nbsp; After just a few minutes, the result looks&nbsp; great. As you can see, both the watermark and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the subtitles have been completely removed. Likewise, if you only need to remove either&nbsp;&nbsp; the watermark or the subtitles,&nbsp; simply choose Option 2 or Option 3. &nbsp; Next, let\'s move on to Option 4:&nbsp; Video Upscaling and Restoration. &nbsp;'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'As you can see, the input video has a very low&nbsp; resolution of just 640 × 720, and the overall&nbsp;&nbsp; quality is quite poor. If we zoom in, the&nbsp; details appear blurry and heavily pixelated. &nbsp;'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'ll keep the test short by processing only&nbsp; the first 125 frames, and upscale the video&nbsp;&nbsp; to 1280 pixels in height. Once everything&nbsp; is configured, I\'ll start the workflow. &nbsp; And here are the results after the&nbsp; restoration, upscaling, and enhancement.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'They look fantastic. The video has been upscaled&nbsp; to HD resolution, and the missing details have&nbsp;&nbsp; been reconstructed remarkably well while&nbsp; preserving the original structure of the image. &nbsp; In my opinion, the quality is on par with many&nbsp; of today\'s paid online video enhancement tools. &nbsp;'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Finally, Options 5 and 6 let me expand my videos&nbsp; by adding content to the sides or the top and&nbsp;&nbsp; bottom, making it easy to convert vertical&nbsp; videos into horizontal ones, or vice versa. &nbsp; Using these options is very straightforward.&nbsp; Simply load a video, check its properties,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'select the duration and the starting frame to&nbsp; process, then enter a brief prompt describing&nbsp;&nbsp; the content. Once everything is set up,&nbsp; just click Run to start the workflow. &nbsp; The workflow will automatically select the&nbsp; appropriate image pre-processing module&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to generate the missing regions for each&nbsp; frame. In this process, the Outpainting&nbsp;&nbsp; LoRA fills in those areas by using both the&nbsp; original video and your prompt as references. &nbsp; As you can see on the screen, the vertical video&nbsp; has been successfully expanded on both sides,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'turning it into a horizontal format. The newly&nbsp; generated content blends in naturally with the&nbsp;&nbsp; original footage, and the overall video quality&nbsp; is excellent. It\'s a really impressive result. &nbsp; Since this is an all-in-one video editing&nbsp; workflow, I\'ve optimized it for the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'highest possible quality by bypassing LTX2.3&nbsp; traditional downscaling and upscaling steps.&nbsp;&nbsp; This means the workflow runs a bit slower, but&nbsp; the visual quality is well worth the trade-off. &nbsp; That\'s all for this video. I hope&nbsp; you find this workflow useful&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:16] [scene:talk]
